# PATCH(nodnarb93): force LF on files whose contents Linux/Drizzle interpret
# byte-exactly. Without this, Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true land
# them with CRLF, which:
#   - prevents Linux from exec'ing shell scripts (#! has \r in the shebang),
#   - and changes the SHA hash of .sql migrations so Drizzle sees every
#     migration as un-applied and crashes recreating existing tables.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
